    "source": "\n**Frame:** Both sides address a channel that would carry an assurance. Left waits on a board message; right waits on a standard, a commitment, or a rival's action. Both channels are drawn, and both are empty.\n\n**Left dialogue — AGENT:**\n> I will hold if the others hold.\n\n**Right dialogue — INSTITUTIONAL ROLE:**\n> We can slow if the field slows with us.\n\n**Caption:**\n> EACH ACTOR WANTS A GUARANTEE IT CANNOT CREATE ALONE.\n\n**Provenance:** `compressed` + `invented` — neither line is a source quotation. The empty channel is the page's subject and must stay visible in every later panel.\n\n",
